{
  "name": "How to Get a Perfect Interior Log Seal",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Want to give your log home interior that perfect, protective seal? It's totally achievable with the right steps! First, and this is crucial, make sure your wood is clean and dry. Like, really dry. We’re talking about getting that moisture level below 18% before you even think about applying anything. If there’s any dirt or dampness, your sealer won't adhere properly, and you'll run into issues down the road. Once your logs are prepped, and if you’re staining, make sure the stain is fully cured, then you can apply your clear coat or sealer. This layer is what protects your beautiful stain and helps lock in the appearance, making your logs easier to maintain. Always apply evenly, and give it enough drying time between coats and for the final cure. Don't rush this part – patience is key for a durable, attractive finish. If you're dealing with older logs that might have some hidden moisture issues, or if you're not sure which products are compatible with previous finishes, that’s when bringing in a professional like HH Remodeling can be super helpful. We can ensure the process is done right, from start to finish, for a truly flawless interior seal.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
